WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.146
Week 18: Irregular Preterite and Meaning Change. report discoveries and attempts distinguish intention from outcome summarize a trip

2
00:00:09.146 --> 00:00:23.287
Form and meaning. Applying the form. Irregular preterite stems change their base and often shift meaning: saber→supe (found out), poder→pude (managed to), querer→quise (tried to).

3
00:00:23.287 --> 00:00:49.075
Model set. No pudimos terminar a tiempo. Quisieron ayudar, pero no tuvieron tiempo. Supimos la noticia esa tarde. Fuimos al pueblo por otra carretera. Dijimos la verdad desde el principio. We couldn't finish on time. They wanted to help, but they didn't have time. We found out the news that afternoon. We went to town by another road. We told the truth from the beginning.

4
00:00:49.075 --> 00:00:59.355
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:59.355 --> 00:01:12.898
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: report discoveries and attempts; distinguish intention from outcome; summarize a trip. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:12.898 --> 00:01:39.540
Model language. No pudimos terminar a tiempo. — We couldn't finish on time. Quisieron ayudar, pero no tuvieron tiempo. — They wanted to help, but they didn't have time. Supimos la noticia esa tarde. — We found out the news that afternoon. Fuimos al pueblo por otra carretera. — We went to town by another road. Dijimos la verdad desde el principio. — We told the truth from the beginning.

7
00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:49.545
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
